10. Hepatic encephalopathy, hepatorenal syndrome or Child-Pugh grade C or more severe cirrhosis, liver failure;
11. Clinically uncontrollable third space effusion, such as pleural fluid and ascites that could not be controlled by drainage or other methods before enrollment;
12. Combined with other serious organic disease or mental illness;
